		{"id":"e35df21a0dab70b1","type":"text","text":"\n| Name                 | Type            | Effect                                                                                                                                 | Visuals                                                                                     | Done?        |\n| -------------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| Gharch Hierophant    | Champion        |                                                                                                                                        | A tall, green-skinned, slouched figure with a large-capped mushroom growing out of its neck | No           |\n| Gharch Fungal Knight | Rare Creature   | Arrival: has 1 Bulwark. When equipping a Ri'Salashor: gain 0/+1.                                                                       |                                                                                             | No           |\n| Gharch Frond Priest  | Rare Creature   | Cast: pay 1 mana and revive a creature from enemy graveyard as an allied Ghoul.                                                        |                                                                                             | No           |\n| Gharch Tender        | Rare Creature   | Cast: put one Ri'Salashor card into your hand.                                                                                         |                                                                                             | No           |\n| Gharch Pilgrim       | Common Creature | Death: put 3 Ri'Salashor cards into your hand.                                                                                         |                                                                                             | No           |\n| Ghoul                | Creature        |                                                                                                                                        | Slobbering ghoul with many fungal growths all over.                                         | No           |\n| Ri' Salahshor        | Ritual          | Bolster one ally +1/+0. Can be produced indefinitely by Tenders.                                                                       | A plant/fungal blade protruding from a Fungal Knight’s arm.                                 | No           |\n| Ri' Arvah            | Rare Ritual     | Exile all creature cards in the graveyard. Summon one ghoul to allied side per card exiled.                                            |                                                                                             | Art done     |\n| Ri' Jan              | Rare Ritual     | Fetch the first Creature card from you deck. If it is an allied card, put it into your hand. If it is an enemy card, exile it instead. | A close-up of a Fungal-knight with glowing eyes.                                            | Systems Done |\n| Ri' Pasar            | Rare Ritual     | Transform 1 allied creature into a Pasar.                                                                                              | A person melting into a green blob of algae                                                 | Done         |\n| Pasar                | Creature        |                                                                                                                                        | A green blob of algae.                                                                      | Done         |\n","x":-490,"y":180,"width":1030,"height":680},
		{"id":"1171bfaf35371087","type":"text","text":"Main Mechanics: Necromancy, Transformation.\nWeaknesses: Low offense, situational abilities, expensive cards.","x":-420,"y":-80,"width":403,"height":117},
		{"id":"258830d383a8344e","type":"text","text":"Types: Warrior, Priest, Commoner.","x":180,"y":-51,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1c3abc8add73cef3","type":"text","text":"The Gharch are immotal mystics who people the base of an ancient ziggurat called Mozar. The Gharch of the deep jungles believe that in life, one must see themselves as dead. Thinking that, they place fungal fronds brought from the Cloying Green Hell on their skin, so that they might take their bodies over in time of their natural failure, and through that, make them immortal. Hidden from men, deep inside the jungle, they guard an ancient ziggurat, whose inner dimensions are beyond anyone's ken. The greatest secret of that ziggurat, and the most hushedly spoken-about, is that inside sleeps a gigantic Dactylos known as Maolmona, the only survivor of the betrayed mangrove-sun, who would wake if some force should dare to threaten the jungle.","x":742,"y":172,"width":538,"height":328},
		{"id":"db7773d47ca21e04","type":"text","text":"With their speaking style, it could be cool to have it run the gamut from normal to eldritch and barely-understandable, like Mycon from Star Control 2. This should show the degrees they are influenced by Maolmona. Failing that, just make them full Mycon.\n","x":741,"y":547,"width":579,"height":133},
		{"id":"3745628455d51c28","type":"text","text":"Among the Gharch, there exist many unlives, which is what a foreigner might call their existence. Every caste has its own unlife, with what perks and limitations that are appropriate to its station, dictated by the strain of the mushroom they host.\n\nThe Gharch are feared as adversaries, for their warriors seldom stay dead unless completely mangled. For those of enemy's kin who fall to their wrath, their priests have the basest frond of all, the Arvah, which raises their fresh corpses as ever-slobbering, wretched, hungry husks.","x":1320,"y":172,"width":625,"height":237}
